Package: nuc-ec-hwmon-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 2.1.0.0)
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-amd64 | linux-headers
Description: hwmon driver for the Intel NUC embedded controller (DKMS)
 Publishes an Intel NUC's fan tachometer and EC temperature bytes as an
 ordinary hwmon device, so lm-sensors and node-exporter can read them. The NUC
 exposes no fan through any standard interface: there is no Super I/O at the
 usual ports, and the ACPI fans are on/off devices carrying no speed.
 .
 The driver reads through the kernel's own ACPI EC path, never writes to the
 EC, and refuses to bind unless both a known board layout and the EC's
 "NUC_EC" signature check out.
 .
 DKMS rebuilds the module on every kernel upgrade; without that the sensors
 would silently vanish after the next reboot.
